          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"}> pre
            \-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            %em with defects
            is, roughly a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            that assigns data not just to plain
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            field theory may then undergo transitions.
          %p
            Such defects are known by many names. In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            1 they are often called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+walls"} domain walls
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundaries"} boundaries
            they are often called
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-branes"} bi-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"} Wilson lines
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+strings"} cosmic strings
            (at least in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#DefinitionGeneral General
          %p
            A plain
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            field theory) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-functor"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-functor"} (∞,n)-functor
            from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"} (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z : Bord_n \to \mathcal{C}^\otimes
                  \\,.
          %p
            If one replaces plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            here with cobordisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                    %mi Def
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n^{Def}
            “with singularities” including
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundaries"} boundaries
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/corners"} corners
            but also partitions labeled in a certain index set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Def
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Def
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                    %mi Def
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z : Bord_n^{Def} \to \mathcal{C}
          %p
            a TQFT
            = succeed "." do
              %em with defects
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie 09, section 4.3
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "cobordism+hypothesis#ForCobordismsWithSingularities"} Cobordism theorem – For cobordisms with singuarities (boundaries/branes and defects/domain walls)
            %a{:href => "#DavydovRunkelKong11"} Davydov, Runkel &amp; Kong 2011
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#CarquevilleRunkelSchaumann"} Carqueville-Runkel-Schaumann
          %p Such a morphism carries data as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for each label in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Def
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Def
                of codimension 0 there is an ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
                field theory;
            %li
              %p
                for each label in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Def
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Def
                of codimension 1 data on how to “connect” the two TQFTs on both sides
            %li
              %p etc.
          %p
            So one may think of the codimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            colors as
            %em defects
            where the TQFT that one is looking at changes its nature.
          %p
            In particular, when the QFT on one side of the defect is trivial, then the defect behaves like a
            %em boundary condition
            for the remaining QFT. Since at least for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=2
            QFT such boundary conditions are also called
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bi-branes"} bi-branes
          %p
            The statement of the
            %strong cobordism theorem with singularities
            (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie09"}> Lurie 09, theorem 4.3.11
            ) is essentially the following:
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,n)-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^\otimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphisms"} k-morphisms
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Def
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Def
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                    %mi Def
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n^Def
            is the free symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                    %mi Def
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Bord_n^Def)^\otimes \to \mathcal{C}^\otimes
            are equivalently given by realizing such a pasting diagram in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-morphism"} k-morphism
            appears as the value of a codimension
            = succeed "-defect." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-k)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie09"} Lurie 09, remark 4.3.14
          %h3#DefectsFromBrokenSymmetry Topological defects from spontaneously broken symmetry
          %p
            An old notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/defects"} defects
            in field theory – well preceding the
            %a{:href => "#DefinitionGeneral"} above
            general notion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            – is that of
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+defects"} topological defects
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
              structure of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
              that exhibit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneous symmetry breaking
              (such as a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+mechanism"} Higgs mechanism
          %p
            A comprehensive review is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#VilenkinShellard94"} Vilenkin &amp; Shellard 1994
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#PreskillVilenkin92"} Preskill &amp; Vilenkin 1992
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFT"} FQFT
            definition
            %a{:href => "#DefinitionGeneral"} above
            along the lines of
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaValentino"} Fiorenza &amp; Valentino
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#FSS"} FSS
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            of some
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \hookrightarrow G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of global symmetries preserved by some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            configuration (which “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"}> spontaneously breaks
            ” the symmetry from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+mechanism"} Higgs mechanism
          %p
            Then the space of such vacuum configurations is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
            space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"}> spacetime
            ),
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            configuratons are given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to G/H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H_1
            is the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of vacua” or “vacuum space” in this context.
          %p
            The functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to G/H
            are to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            of spacetime. If they are allowed to be non-smooth or even non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
            along given strata of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong defects
            in the sense of broken gauge symmetry.
          %p
            In particular (with counting adapted to
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim X = 4
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to G/H
                is not smooth but is smooth on the pre-image of each element of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(G/H)
                and becomes a smooth function on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X-S_1
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1 \hookrightarrow X
                is a
                = succeed "-1" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_1
                is said to be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+wall"} domain wall
                for vacuum configurations.
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to G/H
                is not smooth but becomes smooth on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X-S_2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_2
                is a codimension-2 submanifold, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_2
                is calld a
                = succeed "-defect" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+string"} cosmic string
            %li
              %p
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to G/H
                is not smooth but becomes smooth on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X-S_3
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_3
                is a codimension-3 submanifold, then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_3
                is calld a
                = succeed "-defect" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
          %blockquote
            %p hm, need to fine-tune the technical conditions here, to make the following statement come out right…
          %p So
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+walls"} domain walls
                can appear when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(G/H)
                is non-trivial;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+strings"} cosmic strings
                can appear when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(G/H)
                is non-trivial;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
                can appear when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_2(G/H)
                is non-trivial.
          %p
            Next consider a sequence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_2 \hookrightarrow H_1 \hookrightarrow H_0 \coloneqq G
          %p
            to be thought of as coming from two consecutive steps of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneous symmetry breaking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_1
            at some
            = succeed "-scale" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo &lt;
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2 \lt E_1
          %p
            Then we say that vacuum defects at energy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
            of codimension-
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            which wind around an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_k(H_1/H_2)
            are
            %strong metastable
            if they become unstable at energy
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_k(H_0/H_2)
            is trivial.
          %p
            So if we add to the singular cobordism category the
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-dimenional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ball"} ball
            removed, then the boundary field data for metastable codimension
            = succeed "-defects" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi k
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  [0,1]^k - D^k &amp;\to &amp; \Pi(H_1/H_2)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  [0,1]^k &amp;\to&amp; \Pi(H_0/H_2) &amp;\to&amp; \Pi(H_0/H_1)
                  }
          %p
            we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+sequence"} homotopy fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Pi(H_1/H_2) \to \Pi(H_0/H_2) \to \Pi(H_0/H_1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This induces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+of+homotopy+groups"} long exact sequence of homotopy groups
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \to \pi_{k+1}(H_0/H_1) \to \pi_k(H_1/H_2) \to \pi_k(H_0/H_2) \to \pi_k(H_0/H_1)
                  \\to
                  \\pi_{k-1}(H_1/H_2) \to \cdots
                  \\,.
          %p
            So for every metastable defect of codimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-k
            given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in ker(\pi_k(H_1/H_2) \to \pi_k(H_0/H_2))
            there is an element in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_{k+1}(H_0/H_1)
            of one codimension higher. One says (
            %a{:href => "#PreskillVilenkin92"}> Preskill &amp; Vilenkin 1992
            ) that the codimenion
            = succeed "-defect" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-k)
            = succeed "-defect." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mi k
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-k-1)
          %p (…)
          %p
            In order to formalize this we introduce, following the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theorem"} cobordism theorem
            with singularities, cells in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Span
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Span_n(\mathbf{H})
            which label spontaneous-symmetriy-breaking defects as well as their defects-of-defects which exhibit their decay by higher codimension defects.
          %p Consider a span of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  [\Pi(S^{k-1}), \Pi(H_1/H_2)]
                  \&amp;\leftarrow&amp;
                  [\Pi(S^{k-1}), \Pi(H_1/H_2)]
                  \&amp;\rightarrow&amp;
                  \\ast
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Comparing this to the span that comes from the “cap”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi k
                  %mo ←
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{k-1} \to D^{k} \leftarrow \emptyset
            in the theory at energy level
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  [\Pi(S^{k-1}), \Pi(H_1/H_2)]
                  \&amp;\leftarrow&amp;
                  [\Pi(D^{k}), \Pi(H_1/H_2)]
                  \&amp;\rightarrow&amp;
                  \\ast
                  }
          %p
            shows that the former models a
            = succeed "-disk" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
            In order to formalize how these defects may decay at higher energy, consider next a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            configurations of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mo *
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  [\Pi(S^{k-1}), \Pi(H_1/H_2)]
                  \&amp;\leftarrow&amp;
                  [\Pi(S^{k}), \Pi(H_0/H_1)]
                  \&amp;\rightarrow&amp;
                  [\ast, \Pi(H_0/H_2)]
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Comparing again to the span that comes from the “cap”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi k
                  %mo ←
                  %mi ∅
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{k-1} \to D^{k} \leftarrow \emptyset
            in the theory at energy level
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_2
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi H
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
