          %h4#in_2d_field_theory In 2d field theory
          %p
            Defects in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-dimensional+conformal+field+theory"} 2-dimensional conformal field theory
            have a long history in real-world application, for instance in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kramers-Wannier+duality"} Kramers-Wannier duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
            via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FRS+theorem+on+rational+2d+CFT"} FRS theorem on rational 2d CFT
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#FRS04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrg+Fr%C3%B6hlich"}> Jürg Fröhlich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"} Jürgen Fuchs
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Runkel"} Ingo Runkel
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
              = succeed "," do
                %em Kramers-Wannier duality from conformal defects
              %strong 93
              (2004) 070601 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.93.070601"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.93.070601
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/0404051"} arXiv:cond-mat/0404051
          %p with a comprehensive review in
          %ul
            %li#FFRS07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrg+Fr%C3%B6hlich"}> Jürg Fröhlich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"} Jürgen Fuchs
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Runkel"} Ingo Runkel
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
              = succeed "," do
                %em Duality and defects in rational conformal field theory
              %strong 763
              (2007) 354-430 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0607247"}> arXiv:hep-th/0607247
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.11.017"} doi:10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2006.11.017
          %p
            Realization in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+field+theory"} lattice field theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                David Aasen, Roger S. K. Mong, Paul Fendley,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological Defects on the Lattice I: The Ising model
                %strong 49
                (2016) 354001 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1601.07185"}> arXiv:1601.07185
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1751-8113/49/35/354001"} doi:10.1088/1751-8113/49/35/354001
            %li
              %p
                David Aasen, Paul Fendley, Roger S. K. Mong,
                %em Topological Defects on the Lattice: Dualities and Degeneracies
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.08598"}> arXiv:2008.08598
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1812559"} inspire:1812559
            %li
              %p
                Mao Tian Tan, Yifan Wang, Aditi Mitra,
                %em Topological Defects in Floquet Circuits
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.06272"}> arXiv:2206.06272
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and simulation on a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+computer"} quantum computer
          %ul
            %li
              Sutapa Samanta, Derek S. Wang, Armin Rahmani, Aditi Mitra,
              %em Isolated Majorana mode in a quantum computer from a duality twist
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.02387"}> arXiv:2308.02387
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Defects in 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theory"} topological field theory
            have been studied a lot in the context of genus-0 TFT, where they are described using the language of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+algebras"} planar algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/09/planar_algebras_tfts_with_defe.html"} Planar Algebras, TFTs with Defects
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Carqueville"}> Nils Carqueville
              ,
              %em Lecture notes on 2-dimensional defect TQFT
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1607.05747"}> arXiv:1607.05747
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p On the derivation of the relevant topological term in 2d theories with defects through the use of bi-branes and inter-bi-branes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Runkel"}> Ingo Runkel
                , Rafal R. Suszek.
                %em Gerbe-holonomy for surfaces with defect networks
                (2008). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0808.1419"}> arXiv:0808.1419
                ).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"}> Jürgen Fuchs
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Konrad+Waldorf"} Konrad Waldorf
                %em Bundle Gerbes and Surface Holonomy
                (2009). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.2085"}> arXiv:0901.2085
                ).
            %li
              %p
                Rafal R. Suszek.
                %em Defects, dualities and the geometry of strings via gerbes. I. Dualities and state fusion through defects
                (2011). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1101.1126"}> arXiv:1101.1126
                ).
            %li
              %p
                Rafal R. Suszek.
                %em Defects, dualities and the geometry of strings via gerbes II. Generalised geometries with a twist, the gauge anomaly and the gauge-symmetry defect
                (2012). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1209.2334"}> arXiv:1209.2334
                ).
          %p Defects in Landau-Ginburg theory:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilka+Brunner"}> Ilka Brunner
                , Daniel Roggenkamp.
                %em B-type defects in Landau-Ginzburg models
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0707.0922"}> arXiv:0707.0922
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Carqueville"}> Nils Carqueville
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Murfet"} Daniel Murfet
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Adjunctions and defects in Landau-Ginzburg models
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1208.1481"} arXiv:1208.1481
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Carqueville"}> Nils Carqueville
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Runkel"} Ingo Runkel
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Orbifold completion of defect bicategories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1210.6363"} arXiv:1210.6363
          %h4#in_chernsimons_theory In Chern-Simons theory
          %ul
            %li
              An old example is the class of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Turaev-Reshetikhin+TQFT"} Turaev-Reshetikhin TQFT
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
              with codimension 3 and 2 defects. This is supposed to be the would-be result of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"} Wilson lines
              in this context.
          %p
            Defects in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            and related systems are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"}> Davide Gaiotto
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                %em S-Duality of Boundary Conditions In N=4 Super Yang-Mills Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0807.3720"}> arXiv:0807.3720
                )
            %li
              %p
