            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ilka+Brunner"}> Ilka Brunner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Carqueville"} Nils Carqueville
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Roggenkamp"} Daniel Roggenkamp
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Truncated affine Rozansky-Witten models as extended defect TQFTs
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.06284"} arXiv:2307.06284
          %h4#TopologicalDefectsInGaugeTheories Topological defects in gauge theories with broken symmetry
          %p
            The following references discuss the traditional notion of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+defects"} topological defects
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
              structure of gauge theory with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spontaneous+symmetry+breaking"} spontaneous symmetry breaking
            such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain+walls"} domain walls
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmic+strings"} cosmic strings
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+defects"} topological defects
            of higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
          %ul
            %li#PreskillVilenkin92
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Preskill"}> John Preskill
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Vilenkin"} Alexander Vilenkin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Decay of Metastable Topological Defects
                %strong 47
                (1993) 2324-2342 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/9209210"}> arXiv:hep-ph/9209210
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.47.2324"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.47.2324
            %li#VilenkinShellard94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Vilenkin"}> Alexander Vilenkin
                , E. P. S. Shellard:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmic strings and other topological defects
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/us/universitypress/subjects/physics/theoretical-physics-and-mathematical-physics/cosmic-strings-and-other-topological-defects?format=PB&isbn=9780521654760"} ISBN:9780521654760
            %li
              %p
                Minoru Eto, Youichi Isozumi, Muneto Nitta, Keisuke Ohashi, Norisuke Sakai.
                %em Instantons in the Higgs Phase
                (2004). (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412048"}> arXiv:hep-th/0412048
                ).
          %h4#in_solid_state_physics In solid state physics
          %p
            Defects field theory motivated from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#KitaevKong11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Kitaev"}> Alexei Kitaev
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liang+Kong"} Liang Kong
              %em Models for gapped boundaries and domain walls
              Commun. Math. Phys. 313 (2012) 351-373 (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1104.5047"}> arXiv:1104.5047
              )
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesVortexAnyons Defect anyons
            %p
              Often the concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyons"} anyons
              is introduced as if a generalization of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle+statistics"} particle statistics
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quanta"} quanta
              like fundamental
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosons"} bosons
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/soliton"} solitonic
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/defects"} defects
              such as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vortices"} vortices
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              phases are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} adiabatic
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+phases"} Berry phases
            %p
              The general concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/defects"} defects
              in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            %ul
              %li#Mermin79
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N.+David+Mermin"}> N. David Mermin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The topological theory of defects in ordered media
                %strong 51
                (1979) 591
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.51.591"} doi:10.1103/RevModPhys.51.591
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    (including a review of
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Topology+--+2"} basic homotopy theory
            %p
              and more specifically for
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vortices"} vortices
            %ul
              %li#LoPreskill93
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hoi-Kwong+Lo"}> Hoi-Kwong Lo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Preskill"} John Preskill
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Non-Abelian vortices and non-Abelian statistics
                %strong 48
                (1993) 4821 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.48.4821"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.48.4821
                ]
            %p
              Explicit discussion as defect
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyons"} anyons
            %ul
              %li#Kitaev06
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexei+Kitaev"}> Alexei Kitaev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anyons in an exactly solved model and beyond
                %strong 321
                1 (2006) 2-111 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aop.2005.10.005"}> doi:10.1016/j.aop.2005.10.005
                ]
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}
                    [p. 4:] “
                    %em> Anyonic particles are best viewed as a kind of topological defects that reveal nontrivial properties of the ground state.
                    ”
            %p
              and with focus on defect
              = succeed ":" do
                %a{:href => "braid+group+statistics#ReferencesAnyonicBraidingInMomentumSpace"} anyons in momentum space
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anyonic topological order in TED K-theory
                %strong 35
                03 (2023) 2350001 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X23500010"}> doi:10.1142/S0129055X23500010
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2206.13563"} arXiv:2206.13563
            %p#ReferencesGenons
              Anyonic defects which act as
              = succeed "," do
                %strong genons
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
              of the ambient 2D
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maissam+Barkeshli"}> Maissam Barkeshli
                  ,
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Liang+Qi"} Xiao-Liang Qi
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Topological Nematic States and Non-Abelian Lattice Dislocations
                  %strong 2
                  031013 (2012) [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevX.2.031013"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevX.2.031013
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.3311"} arXiv:1112.3311
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maissam+Barkeshli"}> Maissam Barkeshli
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chao-Ming+Jian"} Chao-Ming Jian
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Liang+Qi"} Xiao-Liang Qi
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Twist defects and projective non-Abelian braiding statistics
                  %strong 87
                  (2013) 045130 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.87.045130"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.87.045130
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1208.4834"} arXiv:1208.4834
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Liang+Qi"}> Xiao-Liang Qi
                  \:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Defects in topologically ordered states
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://nationalmaglab.org/media/dlpayc5u/qi_1.pdf"} pdf
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Qi-DefectsInTopologicalOrder.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maissam+Barkeshli"}> Maissam Barkeshli
                  ,
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Freedman"} Michael Freedman
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Modular transformations through sequences of topological charge projections
                  %strong 94
                  (2016) 165108 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.94.165108"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.94.165108
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1602.01093"} arXiv:1602.01093
            %p
              and specifically in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+Hall+systems"} quantum Hall systems
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maissam+Barkeshli"}> Maissam Barkeshli
                  ,
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Xiao-Liang+Qi"} Xiao-Liang Qi
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Synthetic Topological Qubits in Conventional Bilayer Quantum Hall Systems
                  %strong 4
                  (2014) 041035 [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevX.4.041035"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevX.4.041035
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1302.2673"} arXiv:1302.2673
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrey+Gromov"}> Andrey Gromov
                  \:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Geometric Defects in Quantum Hall States
                  %strong 94
                  085116 (2016) [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.94.085116"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.94.085116
                  ]
            %p see also:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Burton"}> Simon Burton
                , Elijah Durso-Sabina, Natalie C. Brown:
                %em Genons, Double Covers and Fault-tolerant Clifford Gates
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.09951"}> arXiv:2406.09951
                ]
            %p and their potential experimental realization:
            %ul
              %li
                Zhao Liu, Gunnar Möller, Emil J. Bergholtz:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Exotic Non-Abelian Topological Defects in Lattice Fractional Quantum Hall States
                %strong 119
                (2017) 106801 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.106801"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.106801
                ]
            %p
              Concrete
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vortex"} vortex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mphantom
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phantom{-}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyons"} anyons
              in
              = succeed ":" do
